# Pack files are maps, not text (PACK-SPEC.md in KodeStar/audiosilo-meta). git's
# line merge can apply two branches' insertions of the SAME entry key at
# different anchors and leave the key in the file twice, which is not valid pack
# storage - pkg/pack refuses it and metafmt cannot re-render it.
# scripts/pack-union-merge.sh merges the entry maps instead, with the same
# three-way rules a person would apply, so name it here as the merge driver for
# the data tree. In this repository the family is works-community, whose rule is
# the disjoint-member union: a characters pull request and a recaps pull request
# for the same work merge, and a member both sides wrote is a refusal.
#
# A driver only runs where it is configured, which keeps this additive: the
# intake workflow configures it, a contributor can with
#
#   git config merge.packjson.name "three-way merge of pack-file entries"
#   git config merge.packjson.driver "scripts/pack-union-merge.sh %O %A %B %P"
#
# and any checkout that has not falls back to git's own line merge exactly as
# before.
#
# Core carries one more line here, unsetting the attribute for
# data/redirects.json (the slug tombstone table, which is no pack). This
# repository holds no such file - the community tree is one family and nothing
# else - so there is nothing to exempt.
/data/**/*.json merge=packjson
